==Ancient Greek==

===Alternative forms===
* {{grc-alt|κλέϝος|dial=pho}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|grc|κλέϝος}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|grc}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱléwos}}. Cognates include Sanskrit {{m|sa|श्रवस्|tr=śrávas|sc=Deva}}, Avestan {{m|ae|𐬵𐬀𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬯|tr=sravah}}, Old Armenian {{m|xcl|լու|}}, {{m|xcl|լսեմ|}}, Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|слово|tr=slovo|sc=Cyrs}}, and Old Irish {{m|sga|clú}}. Compare {{m|grc|κλύω||I hear}} and {{m|grc|κλέω}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|w=κλέος}}

===Noun===
{{grc-noun|κλέους|n|third}}

# [[rumour]], [[report]]
# good report, [[fame]], [[glory]]
# {{label|grc|rare}} bad report, [[disrepute]]

====Inflection====
{{grc-decl-3rd-N-εσ-prx|κλέ|κλέ|κλε|notes2={{w|Homeric Greek|Epic}} plural: {{m|grc|κλέᾰ|tr=-}}, {{m|grc|κλεῖα|tr=-}}}}

